<title>UK: Harvey Nichols up on 35 pct H1 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Harvey Nichols up on 35 pct H1 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in upmarket department store Harvey Nichols rose over two percent on Thursday after the group announced a 35 percent jump in first-half profits.</p>
<p>By 0959 GMT the stock was up 8p at 352-1/2p.</p>
<p>Harvey Nichols said first-half pre-tax profits rose to 5.51 million sterling from 4.09 million in the same period a year ago. The company recommended an interim dividend of 1.9 pence versus nil paid last year.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
